["Implementing such a complex system in C might be challenging due to its lower level nature, and this is why many people prefer more high-level languages like Python or JavaScript for such tasks. Here's a simplified example of how you can start with encrypting and decrypting user data using OpenSSL library:

```c
#include <openssl/evp.h>
#include <openssl/rand.h>
#include <string.h>

#define BUFSIZE 1024

void handleErrors(void) { /* Handle error conditions */ }

int encrypt(unsigned char *plaintext, int plaintext_len, unsigned char *key, unsigned char *iv, unsigned char *ciphertext) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX *ctx;
    int len;
    int ciphertext_len;

    if(!(ctx = EVP_CIPHER_CTX_new())) handleErrors();

    if(1 != EVP_EncryptInit_ex(ctx, EVP_aes_256_cbc(), NULL, key, iv))
        handleErrors();

    if(1 != EVP_EncryptUpdate(ctx, ciphertext, &len, plaintext, plaintext_len))
        handleErrors();
    ciphertext_len = len;

    if(1 != EVP_EncryptFinal_ex(ctx, ciphertext + len, &len)) 
        handleErrors();
    ciphertext_len += len;

    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(ctx);

    return ciphertext_len;
}

int decrypt(unsigned char *ciphertext, int ciphertext_len, unsigned char *key, unsigned char *iv, unsigned char *plaintext) {
    EVP_CIPHER_CTX *ctx;
    int len;
    int plaintext_len;

    if(!(ctx = EVP_CIPHER_CTX_new())) handleErrors();

    if(1 != EVP_DecryptInit_ex(ctx, EVP_aes_256_cbc(), NULL, key, iv))
        handleErrors();

    if(1 != EVP_DecryptUpdate(ctx, plaintext, &len, ciphertext, ciphertext_len))
        handleErrors();
    plaintext_len = len;

    if(1 != EVP_DecryptFinal_ex(ctx, plaintext + len, &len)) 
        handleErrors();
    plaintext_len += len;

    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_free(ctx);

    return plaintext_len;
}
```
This is a simplified example. The actual implementation would be more complex including the key derivation (which includes iterations, salt, and stretching), error handling, thread-safe memory management, concurrency control, alert system for suspicious activities etc. 

This also doesn't address the caching theme problem - you might want to use a database like Redis or Memcached in combination with OpenSSL for storing encrypted data along with its IV and salt.
