['Here is a basic implementation of the requirements that you've provided. 

RandomNumberGenerator.java:
```java
import java.security.SecureRandom;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.function.LongSupplier;

public class RandomNumberGenerator {
    private static final SecureRandom SECURE_RANDOM = new SecureRandom();
    private static final Map<Long, Random> SEQUENCES = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public static List<Integer> createSequences(int numSequences, LongSupplier seedFunc) {
        List<Integer> sequences = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < numSequences; i++) {
            long seed = seedFunc.getAsLong() ^ SECURE_RANDOM.nextLong();
            Random random = new Random(seed);
            SEQUENCES.putIfAbsent(seed, random);
            sequences.add(random.nextInt());
        }
        return sequences;
    }

    public static void reseed() {
        for (Map.Entry<Long, Random> entry : SEQUENCES.entrySet()) {
            long seed = entry.getKey();
            Random random = new Random(seed);
            SEQUENCES.put(seed, random);
        }
    }
}
```
SystemCommandExecutor.java:
```java
import java.io.*;

public class SystemCommandExecutor {
    public static void executeAndReadOutputs(String command, String directory) throws IOException {
        File file = new File("path/to/file");

        if (file.exists()) {
            if (!file.delete()) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("Unable to delete the specified file.");
            }
        }

        Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command, null, new File(directory));

        BufferedReader readerOutputs = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
        BufferedReader readerErrors = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getErrorStream()));

        String line;
        while ((line = readerOutputs.readLine()) != null) {
            System.out.println("OUTPUT: " + line);
        }

        while ((line = readerErrors.readLine()) != null) {
            System.err.println("ERROR: " + line);
        }

        int exitCode = 0;

        try {
            exitCode = process.waitFor();
            System.out.println("Exit code: " + exitCode);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            throw new IllegalStateException(e);
        }

        if (exitCode != 0) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Command execution failed with exit code: " + exitCode);
        }
    }
}
``` 

The implementation above is a basic demonstration of the requirements. There are many factors to consider when building such a library, including handling concurrent access, managing seed distribution, logging and tracking usage patterns, integrating with external systems, testing randomness quality etc. The `RandomNumberGenerator` class provides the basis for this task, while the `SystemCommandExecutor` class can be used as a helper in another application that needs to execute system commands. This does not cover all possible scenarios or edge cases and should be further expanded and tested before being deployed.
']

