        if (!rateLimitService.tryAcquire()) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Rate limit exceeded");
        }

        User user = userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow(() -> new UserNotFoundException());
        user.setPasswordHash(passwordHasher.hash(newPass));
        userRepository.save(user);

        kafkaTemplate.send("updates", "Password updated for user: " + id);
        redisConnectionFactory.getConnection().flushDb();

        return "Password updated successfully";
    }
}
```
This is a simplified example and actual implementation would be more complex involving error handling, logging, configuration, testing, etc. Also, security concerns like data encryption at rest and in transit are not included in this code snippet for simplicity but would be necessary for compliance with strict data protection policies. 

