['The following is a high-level overview of how such a service can be implemented using Java Spring Boot framework, Apache Commons library, JUnit for testing, and Spring Cloud for cloud capabilities. 

```java
// The main service class
@Service
public class MediaFileService {

    private final ExternalSystemGateway externalSystemGateway;
    private final CacheManager cacheManager;

    public MediaFileService(ExternalSystemGateway externalSystemGateway, 
                            CacheManager cacheManager) {
        this.externalSystemGateway = externalSystemGateway;
        this.cacheManager = cacheManager;
    }

    // Upload method
    public void uploadFile(MultipartFile file) {
        try {
            externalSystemGateway.uploadToAllExternalSystems(file);
        } catch (ExternalServiceException e) {
            if (cacheManager.hasCached(file)) {
                // Fallback to local cache
                return;
            } else {
                throw new MediaFileUploadException("Failed to upload file", e);
            }
        }
    }

    // Download method
    public Resource downloadFile(String fileId) {
        try {
            return externalSystemGateway.downloadFromAllExternalSystems(fileId);
        } catch (ExternalServiceException e) {
            if (cacheManager.hasCached(file)) {
                // Fallback to local cache
                return Resource;
            } else {
                throw new MediaFileDownloadException("Failed to download file", e);
            }
        }
    }

    // Delete method
    public void deleteFile(String fileId) {
        try {
            externalSystemGateway.deleteFromAllExternalSystems(fileId);
        } catch (ExternalServiceException e) {
            throw new MediaFileDeleteException("Failed to delete file", e);
        }
    }
}
```

In the above service class, `uploadFile`, `downloadFile` and `deleteFile` methods interact with external systems through a `ExternalSystemGateway`. If there is an issue with any of these calls, we try to fall back to the local cache (if it exists). If this also fails, we throw a custom exception for better error handling.

