```java
import java.util.*;

public class DisjointPairIdentifier {
    private List<List<Integer>> disjointPairs;

    public void identifyDisjointPairs(int[] array) {
        // Initialize disjoint pairs
        disjointPairs = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
            List<Integer> pair = new ArrayList<>();

            // Add current element to the pair
            pair.add(array[i]);

            // Add all other distinct elements in the same group
            for (int j = 0; j < array.length; j++) {
                if (j != i && array[i] % 2 == 0 && array[j] % 2 != 0) {
                    pair.add(array[j]);
                }
            }

            // Add the pair to disjoint pairs only if it has more than one element
            if (pair.size() > 1) {
                disjointPairs.add(pair);
            }
        }
    }

    public List<List<Integer>> getDisjointPairs() {
        return disjointPairs;
    }
}
```

To integrate with an external API, you would need to have a class that makes calls to the API. For error handling and retries, you might want to use something like Spring's Retry template or Apache HttpClient. 

