2. Validate OAuth2 access token response JSON:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <json-c/json.h>
#include <string.h>

int validateToken(const char* json) {
    json_object *jobj = json_tokener_parse(json);
    json_object *type, *expiresIn;

    json_object_object_get_ex(jobj, "token_type", &type);
    json_object_object_get_ex(jobj, "expires_in", &expiresIn);

    if (type && expiresIn) {
        const char* typeStr = json_object_get_string(type);
        int expiresInInt = json_object_get_int(expiresIn);

        return strcmp(typeStr, "Bearer") == 0 && expiresInInt > 0;
    } else {
        return 0;
    }
}
```
This C function parses a JSON string using the json-c library. It then checks that both `token_type` is 'Bearer' and `expires_in` is a positive integer. Please note this code doesn't handle memory management or error checking, which would be necessary for production use. 

Remember to include error handling in all parts of your implementation, especially when dealing with network resources. Also, consider the security implications of what you are doing as well. Always sanitize user input and validate it against potential threats before using it.
