["This is a quite large task that cannot be fully achieved in a single code block due to its complexity. Here's an overview of how you could approach this problem. Due to the complexity of this task, this will just provide a high-level design of your service without specific implementation details. 

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

// Import required libraries
const axios = require('axios');
const redis = require('redis');
const circuitBreaker = require('opossum');
const { promisify } = require('util');

// Initialize Redis Client
const client = redis.createClient();
client.on('error', function (err) {
  console.log('Redis error: ' + err);
});

// Promisify the set method for Redis
const redisSetAsync = promisify(client.set).bind(client);

// Implement a Circuit Breaker pattern to handle external services failures
const circuitBreakers = {};
function getCircuitBreaker(serviceName) {
  if (!circuitBreakers[serviceName]) {
    const breaker = new circuitBreaker(() => axios.get('http://' + serviceName), { timeout: 3000 });
    breaker.fallback(() => 'Service unavailable');
    circuitBreakers[serviceName] = breaker;
  }
  return circuitBreakers[serviceName];
}

// Handling external services failures with Redis caching
async function getExternalData(serviceName) {
  try {
    const cachedResponse = await promisify(client.get).bind(client)(serviceName);
    if (cachedResponse) return JSON.parse(cachedResponse);

    const response = await getCircuitBreaker(serviceName).fire();

    // Save the response to Redis with an expiry time of 30 seconds for caching purposes
    redisSetAsync(serviceName, JSON.stringify(response), 'EX', 30);

    return response;
  } catch (err) {
    console.log('Error: ', err);
    return 'Service unavailable';
  }
}
```
In this example, we use Redis as a cache layer for the external services responses to handle their failures and improve performance by reducing network calls. Also, we implemented a Circuit Breaker pattern using opossum library which is used to prevent an application from sending requests to a downstream service when that service is unhealthy or slow.
Please note: It's not possible to provide the full code for this task within this context due to its complexity. You should consider breaking down your task into smaller tasks, implement them one by one, and then integrate them together. Also, make sure to include error handling in each step of your process to ensure the robustness of your system.
