['This task requires a complex design with multiple components including script loading, caching mechanism, distributed rate limiting, service resilience patterns, etc., all of which can't be completely covered in just one code block due to its complexity. However, I will provide a simplified code snippet for the `renderFooterScripts` function and a mockup implementation of the service using Redis cache.

1) renderFooterScripts:
```csharp
public class ScriptObject 
{
    public string Key { get; set; }
    public string Url { get; set; }
    public bool Defer { get; set; }
    public object Metadata { get; set; }
}

public async Task<string> RenderFooterScripts(List<ScriptObject> scripts) 
{
    StringBuilder footerHtml = new StringBuilder();

    foreach (var script in scripts) 
    {
        var scriptContent = await LoadAndLogScriptExecutionAsync(script.Key, script.Url);

        // Add the sanitized content to the HTML footer
        footerHtml.AppendLine($"<script src=\"{scriptContent}\" defer=\"{script.Defer.ToString().ToLower()}\"></script>");
    }

    return footerHtml.ToString();
}
```

2) Caching Mechanism: 
```csharp
public class ScriptCacheService : IScriptCacheService 
{
    private readonly ConnectionMultiplexer _redis;
    private IDatabase db;

    public ScriptCacheService() 
    {
        this._redis = ConnectionMultiplexer.Connect("localhost");
        db = redis.GetDatabase();
    }

    public async Task<string> GetAsync(string key) 
    {
        var cacheItem = await db.StringGetAsync(key);

        if (cacheItem.IsNullOrEmpty) 
            return null;

        // If the item is found in the cache, update its score and return it
        await UpdateScoreAsync(key);
        return cacheItem;
    }

    public async Task SetAsync(string key, string value) 
    {
        await db.StringSetAsync(key, value);

        // When a new item is added to the cache, set its initial score
        await UpdateScoreAsync(key);
    }

    private async Task UpdateScoreAsync(string key) 
    {
        var currentScore = await db.SortedSetScoreAsync("cache", key);

        if (!currentScore.HasValue) return;

        // Increase the score for recently accessed items, but decrease it for older ones
        var newScore = 1 / (DateTimeOffset.UtcNow - currentScore.Value).TotalSeconds;
        await db.SortedSetAddAsync("cache", key, newScore);
    }
}
```
This service uses the StackExchange.Redis library to interact with Redis, and it assumes that you've already setup a Redis instance. It also implements a simple scoring system based on the time of last access for cache eviction policy. Note: This is just a simplified example and doesn't handle all edge cases and complexities such as network failures, expiration policies, etc. For production code, consider using more robust libraries or services that provide these features.
']

